From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 14:59:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Drone: up to 16 steady tones with binaural, monaural and
 isochronic beats, in its own view

A song-wide drone mixed under the music after the song's effects: 16 tones set in Hz or as a note
(following the master tune), each steady, binaural, monaural or isochronic, with a beat in Hz or
synced to the tempo, four band-limited timbres, level and pan. It ducks with the song's sidechain,
gliding per sample, and is saved with the song.

The Drone view (Scale in Song view, or Drone in the Song menu) is laid out like Song view: one row
per tone, mute column on/off, audition column selects, level as a bar in the mode's colour; the gold
knobs set pitch and beat, the select encoder the mode, and pressing it opens the tone's menu.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
